# Build artifacts
*.bin
*.iso
*.o
*.img
*.elf
# The E7 increment-7 census candidate is a COMMITTED fixture (the sidecar
# include_bytes!s it, the cap host test reads it at boot-check time):
# keep the one file the build script regenerates trackable.
!user/sidecar/fixtures/e7_candidate.elf
*.so
*.a
# POSIX-Environments E3 boot image (init built with e3_envs). The shipped
# sidecars.cpio is tracked; this tenant-environment variant is a local/CI build
# artifact only (make x86-iso-e3 -> tests/e3_multi_env_boot_check.sh). Its
# stamps go with it: `sidecars.cpio.digest` (the user/ sources),
# `sidecars.cpio.sha256` (the archive's own bytes) and `sidecars.cpio.stamps`
# (the one pack-run record those two are projections of) ARE tracked -- the
# default x86-iso ships the committed archive and `make x86-iso` verifies all
# three against the tree -- while the E3 archive and its stamps are written by
# the build that makes it, so none of the four belongs in the index.
sidecars_e3.cpio
sidecars_e3.cpio.digest
sidecars_e3.cpio.sha256
sidecars_e3.cpio.stamps

# Rust sidecar workspace build output
user/target/

# Runtime logs
*.log

# Freebuff desktop app state — SQLite db + per-worktree bookkeeping.
# These are live app files, churned on every session; never tracked
# (cleanup M2.83 removed them from the index; see plan doc §10.176/10.177).
.freebuff/

# Compiler plugin
compiler/*.so
compiler/*.dylib

# Disk images
sls_storage.img
sls_storage_rv64.img

# Packet captures
*.pcap

# run-cluster.sh's per-node artefacts: ISOs, disk images, serial logs and the
# pid file. *.iso/*.img above already cover most of it; this catches the
# whole directory including cluster.pids and node<i>.log.
cluster/

# Build-configuration stamps (see the SLS_SOFTMMU block in Makefile)
.build-config.stamp
.build-id.stamp
.sls-frontend.stamp

# ─── Run scratch, not artefacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Redirected guard/build transcripts (live_run.out, rerun3.out, ...) and the
# commit-message drafts kept beside them: records of past runs, read by
# nobody but whoever ran them, and neither build inputs nor test fixtures.
*.out
commit_*_msg.txt

# ─── Local-only helpers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# qemu: a symlink to a QEMU checkout OUTSIDE this repository (the build reads
#   ../qemu, never ./qemu), so committing it would ship a dead absolute path.
# probe_console_run.sh: self-declared "temporary, delete after use" — a
#   diagnostic with this worktree's absolute path hardcoded in it.
# tools/add_intent_standins.sh: the one-shot patcher that added the
#   idle-observer stand-ins to the host tests; its output is committed in the
#   tests themselves, so replaying it now would only append duplicates.
/qemu
/probe_console_run.sh
/tools/add_intent_standins.sh
